@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the build/verify/deploy chain for every proveo image, and why :local and :latest stay distinct
' covers: internal/maintain/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintain_cmd.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/maintainer_surface_test.go
' covers: internal/imagebuild/**
' covers: internal/imagetest/**
' execute order .............. _spec/internal/maintain/build-schedule.puml
'
' 2026-10-16 (MEASURED): KindSidecar is gone from internal/maintain; the
' squid-proxy, egress-proxy and mitmproxy targets left the registry and
' internal/imagebuild/targets.go with the docker+egress backend ("Retire Docker
' egress"). Two kinds remain: base and harness. The egress-proxy ":local beats
' :latest" note below is HISTORY; egressProxyImage and the egress-proxy image
' inspect header are deleted from cmd/proveo.
'
' 2026-10-18 (N9, MEASURED): `proveo build` is no longer hidden. Root help lists
' it as "Build harness image(s) from a proveo checkout", because operator
' messages send people there: a declined preflight build and the agent-pin line
' both name `proveo build <target>`. deploy and test stay hidden — release
' tooling an operator has no reason to run. `proveo targets` is deleted; the
' registry is read only through loadMaintainRegistry (maintain_cmd.go).
' Pinned by TestRootHelpShowsBuildAndKeepsReleaseToolingHidden
' (cmd/proveo/maintainer_surface_test.go).
' 2026-10-20: that visibility is reversed. mise owns the `build` verb
' (`mise run build` → `go run ./cmd/proveo build`). The command stays
' registered and is Hidden, with deploy and test. Root help no longer
' lists it. TestRootHelpHidesMaintainerCommands is the pin.
' 2026-10-28: the verbs moved to cmd/proveo-dev/maintain.go (`mise run build` →
' `go run ./cmd/proveo-dev build`); the consumer CLI registers none of them.
title Maintainer image pipeline — proveo-dev build / test / deploy

actor "Maintainer" as MT

node "Maintainer host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "mise tasks\nbuild · test-defs · deploy" as MISE <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo-dev build|test|deploy\n(internal/maintain)" as CMD <<app>>
  component "internal/manifest\nharness.manifest set" as MAN <<app>>
  component "Registry(ms, defsDir) → []Target\nname · kind · image · defDir\nrepoRoot · suite" as REG <<app>>
  component "imagebuild.BuildTarget (in-process)\ntargets.go Specs[<name>] → buildx" as BUILD <<app>>
  component "internal/imagetest\nTestImage<Suite> · -tags=image" as TEST <<app>>
}

folder "Target kinds" as KINDS <<host>> {
  component "base\nbase · base-node\nbase-node-browser" as KB <<app>>
  component "harness\nfrom images{} — incl. variants\n(claudecode-solidity, -browser)" as KH <<app>>
  component "sidecar — DELETED 2026-10-16\nsquid-proxy · egress-proxy\nmitmproxy" as KS <<error>>
}

cloud "Registry (docker push)" as REGISTRY <<cloud>>

MT ARROW_MAIN MISE
MISE ARROW_MAIN CMD : " ""go run ./cmd/proveo-dev build …"" "
CMD ARROW_MAIN MAN : enumerate defs
MAN ARROW_MAIN REG
REG ARROW_MAIN KINDS : one Target per buildable image
REG ARROW_MAIN BUILD : local → buildx ""--load"" (host arch)
REG ARROW_OPTIONAL TEST : ""proveo test <target>""
BUILD ARROW_CLOUD REGISTRY : deploy → buildx ""--push""\n""PROVEO_PLATFORMS"" (default linux/amd64,linux/arm64)

note right of REG
  **Derived, never hardcoded.** The buildable set comes
  from the manifest ""images"" map plus the bases (the
  fixed sidecar list went 2026-10-16). A variant is
  its own ""Specs"" row in internal/imagebuild/targets.go —
  ""claudecode"" and ""claudecode-solidity"" share one def
  dir and differ by ""Dockerfile"" (mcp/ vs solidity/).
end note

note bottom of BUILD
  Local builds ""--load"" the host platform only, because
  a multi-arch manifest list cannot be loaded into the
  local docker image store. Multi-arch exists only on
  the ""--push"" path.

  Bases are ensured before dependents: ""BuildTarget""
  ensures the row's ""Parent"" first, so
  ""base-node"" exists before claudecode/opencode
  build ""FROM"" it.

  **The agent inside is pinned, not ""@latest"".** Each
  row's ""Pins"" resolve the current release
  (""Builder.AgentVersion"") and
  pass it as a build-arg the Dockerfile installs and
  verifies, so a warm cache cannot keep a stale agent and
  the image labels what it carries
  (_spec/_devops/agent-version-pin.puml). codex is the
  exception: ""CODEX_VERSION"" defaults to ""latest"".

  //HISTORY, deleted 2026-10-16:// **A newer "":local"" beat "":latest"" for the egress-proxy
  sidecar too** (""egressProxyImage"" in cmd/proveo, same
  ""ResolveImage"" rule as the harness image). The sidecar
  compiles ""internal/provider"" into its binary, so a provider
  added in Go is not brokered until ""proveo build egress-proxy""
  — and a plan that named "":latest"" outright kept launching
  the stale published sidecar over that build: the run
  detected the key, sentinel-injected it, allowlisted the
  host, and the vendor answered 401 as if the key were bad.
  ""PROVEO_EGRESS_PROXY_IMAGE"" still overrides outright.
end note

note bottom of TEST
  ""TestPlan"" runs ""go test -tags=image -run
  '^TestImage<Suite>$' ./internal/imagetest/"", where
  Suite is the def dir's base name; a target with no
  ""<Suite>_test.go"" has no test step.

  Image contract suites assert the *runtime* contract —
  non-root default user, baked tooling, seeded defaults,
  entrypoint bridging — against the built image, not the
  source. Grep-the-source assertions are retired
  (see _spec/tests/20-contract.puml).
end note
note bottom of REG
  **Registry order is dependency order, hand-made rather than sorted.**
  Bases, then harnesses by name (the sidecars that came last are gone). Execute order is
  Schedule: bases one at a time, then one concurrent wave, then
  claudecode-solidity after claudecode.

  **Build and deploy answer different questions, so they are different
  plans.** Both emit one in-process ""imagebuild <target> --tag T
  [--push] [--no-cache]"" step (""Command.Run""; ""Argv"" is only its label).
  ""BuildPlan"" leaves the image tagged locally through ""Builder.Build"",
  which ""--load""s a single platform; ""DeployPlan"" rebuilds with
  ""buildx --push"" for ""linux/amd64,linux/arm64"". A plain
  ""docker push"" of a locally built image cannot substitute — it would
  publish one architecture under a manifest the fleet expects to be
  multi-arch. The verify step's ""docker image inspect"" is run quiet because
  its //failure// is the signal, not its output.
end note

note bottom of CMD
  **Target selection has three shapes and one ordering rule.** An explicit
  name, the literal ""all"", or — with no argument on a TTY — a picker:
  type-to-filter, ""Tab"" toggles several (space is reserved for the filter
  query, which is why Tab is the multi-select key), ""Enter"" confirms.

  The chosen set is then returned **in registry order, not in
  Tab-selection order**, because build order matters and the operator's
  click sequence carries no dependency information.
end note


@enduml
